From 6fa3bcf4c178e4aed74ba56e1a18af50e38681a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:28:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Page: typed desktop address, two-step label, protocol 2,
 kept scripts and demo site

The Android app has no host to ask, so the Engine row offers Desktop (another
computer) with an address box (parseDesktopAddress: IPv4, name, bracketed
IPv6, port default 4300, no path or credentials) and the code box; the
address is remembered in the preferences, the code never. Build probes the
address first so the row says no desktop answered, or the desktop would not
let the app in, in words. The host says only {app, protocol 2, requiresCode}
before the code: the chip says Desktop until the welcome, then the name and
cores. A RemoteVersionError and a full desktop have their own sentences.

On a page a host serves the page now keeps the engine and speed test worker
scripts as blobs when the link opens (a fresh engine starts from them), warms
the Setup data plan chunk, and keeps the chosen demo site's files while
Desktop is chosen, so Continue on this device works with the host gone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016zPE7K49ycKieo7wJdrBFN
