From 448d3e9ea0518605eeb9c0a98789609a43805113 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:45:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Page: hand the probe to connectRemote, a host of another
 version is still a host; cross-origin e2e

A host that says another version of the link before its code is still a
desktop: the page offers it and the connection refuses it with a version
error, so the words say to update the app or the host and not that nothing
answered. e2e/desktop-cross-origin.spec.ts: the app's origin and a real host
on another (listed origin, wrong code, unlisted origin, no host, --allow-app);
e2e/desktop-real.spec.ts now expects protocol 2. Both are skipped, with the
reason, until the host in the tree has --allow-origin.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016zPE7K49ycKieo7wJdrBFN
